{"parentUuid":"23fd3f93-b9f1-4947-9a5e-a6836ad3d300","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8742d174-872d-448c-92ec-e890bce686a1","agentId":"a5bd11e325240fbf9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Xz52LLCs4jihFgW3UhECK","type":"tool_result","content":"# API Keys and Setup Requirements for Node Banana\n\nBased on the README, this project requires the following credentials and setup:\n\n## Required API Keys\n\n**Google Gemini API Key** - This is mandatory, as the project uses it for AI image and text generation features.\n\n## Optional API Keys\n\nThe README indicates three additional providers are available in beta:\n\n- **OpenAI API Key** - \"for OpenAI LLM provider\"\n- **Replicate API Key** - Enables \"thousands of open-source models\"\n- **Fal.ai API Key** - Provides \"fast inference for image and video generation\"\n\n## Setup Instructions\n\nCreate a `.env.local` file in the root directory and add your keys:\n\n```\nGEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key\nOPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key\nREPLICATE_API_KEY=your_replicate_api_key\nFAL_API_KEY=your_fal_api_key\n```\n\n## System Requirements\n\n- Node.js 18 or higher\n- npm package manager\n\nThe documentation notes that \"Configure API keys in Project Settings to enable these providers,\" suggesting keys can also be configured through the application's UI after initial setup."}]},"uuid":"1aa47630-c562-464a-ab9c-343384e5868f","timestamp":"2026-03-26T02:51:17.647Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"23fd3f93-b9f1-4947-9a5e-a6836ad3d300","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/robinsonchan/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/.claude/worktrees/peaceful-elgamal","sessionId":"098ed1dc-83c1-4708-8ae1-e74301a62a13","version":"2.1.78","gitBranch":"claude/peaceful-elgamal"}
